# Justified exceptions for scripts/guards/no-integration-names.sh.
# Format: path_regex:line_regex   (split at the first colon; both are ERE, matched
# against the file path and the matched line respectively).
# Keep entries narrow. Each needs a reason comment above it.

# LLM provider hosts are allowed by design (known_llm_hosts in aurora-llm/aurora-config).
# (no entries yet; add e.g.)
# ^crates/aurora-llm/.*:known_llm_hosts

# (P4-GSL) The fake git host of the test kit emulates the two built-in git hosts' API shapes (docs/18
# §Git skill library); it is test support, never shipped, and the core code stays host-neutral.
^crates/aurora-testkit/src/git_host\.rs$:.*
# (P4-GSL) A sample `Link` header in a unit test of the host-neutral pagination parser.
^crates/aurora-registry/src/library\.rs$:gitlab\.example

# (FIX-123, D-215) The table of built-in apps that became connect methods of another app: an upgrade
# shim that moves the connections of installs still holding the old apps. It is the one place the
# core names built-in packages, and it is data, not integration behaviour.
^crates/aurora-registry/src/superseded\.rs$:.*

# Bundled top-10k common-password list (I-11) is data, not integration code.
^services/aurora-api/data/common-passwords\.txt$:.*

# (P4-PRV-1) The previews-domain validator's coarse public-suffix list: `github.io` is a
# public suffix that must never be a previews domain (no real integration code).
^crates/aurora-config/src/validate\.rs$:github\.io
